      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): warn when JSON5 comments are lost on config write",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw parses `openclaw.json` using JSON5, which supports comments. However, when the configuration is modified, the system saves back using standard `JSON.stringify()`, which strips all user-authored comments.\n\n**Issue**: #105683\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe root cause is in `src/config/io.ts` where config writes use `JSON.stringify()` which cannot preserve JSON5 comments.\n\nThis PR implements a warning to notify users when their comments will be lost. The warning is **not** gated on `skipOutputLogs` — comment stripping is a data-loss event that should always be surfaced, even for machine-parseable (`--json`) callers.\n\n## User Impact\n\n### Before\n- Users add comments to `openclaw.json` for documentation\n- Any config modification silently strips all comments\n\n### After  \n- Users receive a clear warning when writing config with JSON5 comments\n- The warning fires regardless of output mode (including `--json` / `skipOutputLogs`)\n- The warning intelligently excludes false positives (URLs in strings)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Runtime Proof — Real Config Mutation\n\n```\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n  BEFORE — config file with JSON5 comments:\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n{\n  // Gateway configuration — selects local mode for development\n  \"gateway\": {\n    \"mode\": \"local\" // runs the gateway on the local machine\n  },\n  /* Plugin block:\n     add extension plugin entries below */\n  \"plugins\": {\n    \"entries\": {}\n  },\n  /**\n   * Multi-line doc-comment style block\n   * describing the agents section.\n   */\n  \"agents\": {\n    \"list\": [\n      { \"id\": \"main\", \"default\": true }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n  Writing config via createConfigIO.writeConfigFile()...\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n  ⚠️  WARN: Config write will strip JSON5 comments from\n  /tmp/.../openclaw.json. Use a separate tool to re-add\n  documentation comments after modifications.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n  AFTER — config file written by JSON.stringify:\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n{\n  \"gateway\": { \"mode\": \"local\" },\n  \"plugins\": { \"entries\": {} },\n  \"agents\": {\n    \"list\": [{ \"id\": \"main\", \"default\": true }]\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"lastTouchedVersion\": \"2026.6.10\",\n    \"lastTouchedAt\": \"2026-07-13T07:07:04.780Z\"\n  }\n}\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n  VERIFICATION:\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n  Warning emitted:     ✅ PASS\n  Comments stripped:   ✅ PASS\n\n  ✅ PROOF SUCCESSFUL\n```\n\n### Implementation\n\n1. **New `hasJSON5Comments()` function** (`src/config/io.ts`):\n   - Strips string literals using regex before checking for comment tokens\n   - Detects `//` and `/*` comment markers outside of strings\n   - Avoids false positives on URLs (`http://`) and string content\n\n2. **Warning logic**:\n   - Fires on every config write when the original has JSON5 comments\n   - NOT gated on `skipOutputLogs` — always surfaced since comment loss is data loss\n   - Provides actionable guidance to users\n\n3. **Comprehensive tests** (`src/config/io.write-config.test.ts`):\n   - **70 tests pass** — covers comment detection, no-comment configs, URL edge cases, and `skipOutputLogs` suppression verifies the warning still fires\n\n### Code Quality\n\n- TypeScript compliant (no `any` types)\n- Format check passes\n- Follows existing patterns\n\n## Related Work\n\nAddresses issue #105683 and builds upon PR #105727 approach.",
